            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0533" n="421" xml:id="pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7389: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-18T14:00:00+08:00">November 18, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 18—6:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>154. Embassy’s 151, November 16, noon. Following telegram has been received from
                    the Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 17, 11 a.m. Embassy’s telegram of November 16, 1 p.m. I am
                            informed by reliable Chinese that night movements of troop trains
                            through Mukden to Shanhaikwan have been occurring for last 3 nights and
                            that as many as 5,000 troops may be involved. He added that preparations
                            are being made for the concentration at Chinchou by November 24 of 1,000
                            railway operatives to take over Shanhaikwan-Peiping Railway in case of
                            necessity. Japanese sources yield little specific information; all agree
                            that the situation is grave and may lead to intervention. An official
                            connected with mission told me that for some time troops have been held
                            in readiness for emergencies.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking, Shanghai and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
